{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>יקרה.</b> From the root קרה (to encounter)." "<b>ודבר.</b> In construct state with [the following word]." "<b>וילך שפי.</b> The words of the Aramaic translator are known, that it means \"alone.\" And behold, שפי לבדו too means alone, without brother or others. Others said that it is like נכאה לכב, from the root שפה, \"his bones were bare.\" But the correct view in my eyes is that it is from the root קול על שפיים, and it is found with yod and also with alef, like the word פתאים. And the meaning is that he went אל שפי, and the word אל is missing, like ויבא ירושלים, and likewise נסעו העם חצרות, and many similar cases. And behold, he practiced divination in his going, for so it is written, and he did not go as time after time to encounter serpents. And behold, here too I have hinted to you a sealed sod."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The lemma is from יקרה (Numbers 23:3); Ibn Ezra derives it from the root לקראתי, i.e., קרה in the sense of meeting/encountering."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:07.486876824Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}